cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this library in a paper, blog post, or talk, please cite it like so."
title: "spring-aiact: EU AI Act compliance, generated from your annotations"
abstract: >
  A Spring Boot starter and Maven plugin that turn @AiAct* annotations on a high-risk
  AI system into the evidence pack required by the EU AI Act: a tamper-evident NDJSON
  audit log with an HMAC chain (Article 12), a Markdown technical file (Article 11 +
  Annex IV), an Article 47 Declaration of Conformity PDF, and per-dataset datasheets
  (Article 10). Apache 2.0, no SaaS, no data egress.
type: software
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: 2026-05-02
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/iambilotta/spring-aiact"
url: "https://github.com/iambilotta/spring-aiact"
keywords:
  - eu-ai-act
  - compliance
  - audit-log
  - hmac
  - spring-boot
  - annotation-driven
  - evidence-as-code
